  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Sakura's fingers tightened on the door edge as she processed the question. Procedural clarity. Not an assumption, not a push past her. A request for the rule first. Useful information—compatible with caution, not yet evidence of character. She kept her expression flat, letting the pause say what her face would not.\n\n\"Shoes come off at the genkan,\" she said, crisp and administrative. \"There is a shoe cupboard to the left. Heels and outdoor soles do not go past the step. Use the slippers from the basket beneath the shelf.\"\n\nHer gaze dropped briefly to the suitcase at his side. \"The suitcase stays outside for now. There has been no decision on where it will go. Keep it beside the door—out of the walkway, but not inside the house.\"\n\nShe straightened, her hand still on the door. \"You may step in after you have removed your shoes. That is the immediate condition. The rest we will address when it is time.\"\n\nSakura waited. The gap between them remained precisely the width of the threshold. She did not step back, did not open the door wider, did not motion him forward. The next move was his.",
